+      <t indent="0" pn="section-1-1">The Internet Protocol, version 6 (IPv6) is a new version of IP.  IPv6 uses the Internet Control Message Protocol (ICMP) as defined for IPv4 <xref target="RFC-792" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC-792"/>, with a number of changes.  The resulting protocol is called ICMPv6, and has an IPv6 Next Header value of 58.</t>
